  "policy": "Explicit production autoOrders on both sides. Independent/default and reserve-planned arms each run scale1, scale0.5 and scale0. Compare a candidate against scale1 in the SAME arm, and also show the scale1 policy difference. Repeated suite baselines always use shipping defaults and are verified as controls.",
  "partitions": [
    "COST<=17: each row against all other frozen teams",
    "exactC17: only exactC17 rows against the other exactC17 opponents"
  ],
  "reserveRule": {
    "status": "confirmed-before-outcomes",
    "rule": "Extend all three fixed counterplans for one arm/scale/shell together only when fewer than two have passed and at least one remaining counter meets point score >=60% and both physical-orientation scores >50%, but its approximate seed-clustered 95% lower bound is <=50%, such that two passes remain possible. Use all64 reserved seeds once, then combine all128 seeds. Never extend clear point/orientation failures, replace teams, or change thresholds."
  },
  "selection": "Prefer scale0.5 if all gates pass; consider scale0 only if scale0.5 fails and scale0 passes. An unresolved new >=90% row holds adoption. Both fail means the mechanism-only hypothesis is insufficient and the milestone remains open. Parent reviews before production adoption.",
